   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "אִיבָּעֵית אֵימָא: לֵית לֵיהּ, וְאִיבָּעֵית אֵימָא: אִית לֵיהּ, מִי לָא אָמַר רַבִּי חֲנִינָא: שָׁחוֹר — אָדוֹם הוּא, אֶלָּא שֶׁלָּקָה? הָכָא נָמֵי, מִלְקָא הוּא דְּלָקֵי.",
   "en": "The Gemara answers: «If you wish, say» that Akavya ben Mahalalel «does not accept» this opinion of Rabbi Abbahu, as he maintains that there are more than four types of blood in a woman. «And if you wish, say» instead that Akavya ben Mahalalel «accepts» Rabbi Abbahu’s exposition, and the apparent contradiction can be resolved as follows: «Didn’t Rabbi Ḥanina say,» with regard to the «black» blood mentioned in the mishna, that it «is» actually «red but» its color «has faded? Here too,» with regard to the green mentioned by Akavya ben Mahalalel, one can say that it was initially red but its color «faded» and turned green."
  }
